  "result": "I fixed it: subcommands now pick up the defaults you set for them in `default_map`.\n\n**The bug:** in `src/click/core.py:391`, a subcommand's context was given the parent's whole `default_map` instead of only the entry under the subcommand's name. So with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"changed\"}}`, the `sub` command looked for `name` at the top level of the map, didn't find it, and fell back to its normal default.\n\n**The fix:** that line is now `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which hands each subcommand its own nested section of the map. This is how Click's documentation describes `default_map` working.\n\n**Checks:**\n- I added a regression test, `test_subcommand_default_map`, in `tests/test_defaults.py`. It passes, but I didn't run it against the old code to confirm it would have failed there.\n- The full test suite passes: 1906 passed, 102 skipped.\n- A standalone script for this exact case now prints the value from `default_map`.\n\n`uv run` couldn't work offline (it tried to download `uv` itself), so the targeted test file and the script ran with `PYTHONPATH=src` against the local Python.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
